    # HERALD'S DISPATCH — TUNNEL JUNCTION 7, MIDWAY SHELF POSTING
    
    ---
    
    **RAVIUM TRADE AUTHORITY RESTRUCTURED UNDER EMERGENCY ACCORD PROVISIONS — ALL ROUTES REMAIN OPEN**
    
    Be it known to all who trade beneath and above the ice: by authority of the Accord, administrative governance of ☽'slew Ravium~ transfers this cycle to The Midnight Claws under emergency redistribution protocols. Fire-core output stands certified at six hundred forty-two units. New chain-of-custody procedures take immediate effect. The routes remain open. Fire enough for all who comply.
    
    ---
    
    The administrative transition follows precedent established during the restructuring of eastern tunnel commerce necessitated by The Mbra∴silentiu, and is further justified by losses sustained during prior hostilities at the upper terraces. Senior Signatory Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon of Aureate has applied his trade-seal — certifying current fire-core yield figures and confirming route authority reallocation as consistent with Accord provisions. All ceremonies of recognition for outgoing and incoming operators will be conducted at a time and venue appropriate to current conditions.
    
    The Cell, prior operator of ☽'slew Ravium~, receives formal acknowledgment for contributions to deep-route maintenance during the contested period. Standing claims filed through proper channels remain under review. Their guild designation carries continued recognition by Aureate auditors, and their members retain passage rights through established corridors pending compliance with updated regulations.
    
    Glow-Trader Vemlaus-vel~, whose brokerage of cross-cultural commerce frameworks serves as historical authority for trade transfer provisions, confirms that Ravium's quarterly shipment schedules to Aurora Stack heating stations will proceed uninterrupted. "The weight moves. The warmth follows. Compliance ensures both," Vemlaus-vel~ states for the record, her demonstrated loyalty to inter-colony commerce well established.
    
    New regulations take effect immediately: no fire-core may be moved without witnessed chain-of-custody documentation. Forge access at ☽'slew Ravium~ requires authorization from Midnight Claws station-masters. Distribution of fire-craft knowledge outside sanctioned guild channels constitutes grounds for reassignment to deep-work. All shipments above the third depth require armed escort, details posted at Midway Shelf.
    
    ---
    
    Traders and laborers should note: orca war-pod activity along the eastern shore approaches has intensified. The consolidation of Ravium's operations under single management serves defense coordination — disruptions to flow cannot be tolerated while the Berg faces threats that render factional grievance a luxury no colony can afford. Aureate's continued viability as trade auditor ensures restored operations proceed under measurement and witness. Couriers carrying this dispatch bear the seal of both civilizations. Compliance is not requested. The routes remain open.
    
    *— Filed by Negotiator Silvtotuius-obscur~, on behalf of the Shadow Parliament. Carried under courier seal.*
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771586745513_0", anchor: "emergency redistribution protocols", text: "There is no emergency redistribution clause in the ratified Flipper Accord. There is one in the second secret draft — I found it in administrative ice so deep it had turned cobalt. That draft was struck before the public signing. Someone involved in this transfer is citing a provision that officially does not exist. I flagged the same phantom clause surfacing in Zhachelang's provisional allocation authority. Twice now. A struck provision that keeps getting enforced is not struck. It is merely unratified, which is a different thing entirely, and far more useful to those who wield it.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771586745513_1", anchor: "orca war-pod activity along the eastern shore approaches has intensified", text: "Notice what's missing. Any penguin at Tunnel Junction 7 could describe an orca raid in their sleep — shore-breakers driving channels through the ice edge, herders pushing groups toward killing zones, finishers circling below every escape route, hunt-songs vibrating through the ice at frequencies that loosen your grip on your own bones. The dispatch provides none of this. It is not a military advisory. It is a seizure notice that invokes the orca as rhetorical cover. 'Factional grievance a luxury' — dissent reclassified as disloyalty. The oldest trick on the Berg, and it works every time because the teeth are real.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771586745513_2", anchor: "Distribution of fire-craft knowledge outside sanctioned guild channels constitutes grounds for reassignment to deep-work", text: "The Firekeeper Doctrine, unnamed but fully operational. 'Reassignment to deep-work' — a euphemism so thin I can read the ice through it.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
